---
description: In-buffer remux seeks must not restart ffmpeg or drop MSE
alwaysApply: true
---

# Remux seek

An in-buffer remux seek is `video.currentTime` only.

- Clock the buffer from `startAt` (`rel = next - startAt`), then `clampBuffered`.
- Hit → set `currentTime` and stop.
- `setStartAt` / new `t=` / new ffmpeg / new MediaSource only when the target is **outside** the buffer.

Do not point in-buffer seeks at a measured keyframe, tfdt origin, or any clock other than `startAt`. That misses the range, remuxes, and drops the buffer. Subtitle sync must not touch this path.
